# Check every text file out with LF on all three platforms. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true — the GitHub Actions windows image sets it
# system-wide — which would hand `templ generate` CRLF .templ sources; templ
# bakes those \r\n into the generated Go string literals, so the tree goes dirty
# mid-build and `git describe --dirty` stamps the release binary "-dirty".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending-convert these, whatever the content sniffer decides.
*.docx binary
*.ico  binary
*.odt  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.syso binary
